I am a C. elegans geneticist studying developmental biology. I have performed a forward genetic screen to identify mutants that are missing the male specific MCM neurons. MCM neurons are normally derived from the division of amphid socket(AMso) glial cells during larval stage of sexual maturation. drp1(the causal gene we are finding) is a Class III mutation - The AMso divides symmetrically to generate two glial cells instead of the MCM.
